+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+The registry applies each tool's declared JSON Schema before execution so malformed model calls become readable tool results while valid calls retain their original input.
+
+## Registry contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` describing required, type, or enum failures before invoking the executor; error text and logs identify the property and constraint without exposing property values, valid input including extra properties reaches the executor unchanged, and an unknown tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`. ([validated by: validates model input before execution and preserves accepted input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L20))
+- Registering a static tool compiles its schema immediately, names the tool if compilation fails, and reuses the compiled schema across calls. ([validated by: compiles a static schema at registration and reuses it](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L68))
+- A function-valued definition is resolved for each call and each resolved schema object is validated independently. ([validated by: uses the current schema from a function-valued definition](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L91))
+- A rejected tool call is returned to the model as a tool result so it can correct the input in a later round, within the configured tool-round limit. ([validated by: lets the model correct a rejected tool call](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L13))
